  "Number": 14,
  "Question": "When four gallons are added to a tank that is one-third full, the tank is then one-half full. The capacity of the tank in gallons is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\)",
    "B": "\\(12\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(24\\)",
    "E": "\\(48\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "The four added gallons fill the difference between one-half and one-third of the tank. That fraction is\n\\[\n\\frac12-\\frac13=\\frac36-\\frac26=\\frac16.\n\\]\nThus one-sixth of the tank holds \\(4\\) gallons. A full tank contains six of these equal portions, so its capacity is\n\\[\n6\\cdot4=24\\text{ gallons}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(24\\) gallons, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
